{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-solving", "file": "references/periodic-task-345b5b06-review.md", "content": "# Heterogeneous periodic-pattern task lessons

Task task-345b5b06 supplied structurally diverse demos: horizontal monochrome bands expanded into a palette cycle; diagonal marker tracks producing period-5/6 tilings; a period-6 horizontal/vertical pattern; a few-cell checkerboard completion; and a 9x9 band task where blank rows inherited an apparent surrounding color sequence. These examples did not establish one common transformation, and the 25x25 test comprised isolated full-width bars (3, 7, 9, 1) amid blanks. Applying a diagonal-derived cycle to the entire test was unjustified; the submitted grid was speculative and no correctness feedback was received.

